# {{PRODUCT}} — Gemini CLI / Antigravity

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; the kernel wins.

- Phone E2E: `.agents/workflows/phone-e2e.md`; unit tests cannot substitute.
- Use routed follow-up reviewers/carries. Follow NEXT_ACTION; if missing, `task status --task-id <id> --next --brief --json`. Never poll.
- Never advise disabling hooks, hardcoding caps or declaring UI PASS from unit tests.

- Python: `{{PY}}`
- Assemble: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble`
- Harness Execution Boundary: Installed harness engine source under `.agents/scripts/**` is an implementation detail. Execute documented commands directly; do not inspect or recursively read harness Python implementation before execution.
- Device: {{DEVICE_POLICY}}
- Discovery: Graph-backed. Exact code target -> `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` or `--symbol <name>`. Feature/unknown target or cross-module refactor -> `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py graph --feature <name> --json` (or `--find <symbol>`) first, then Task Context on resolved target. Search is never the initial code discovery anchor; after discovery, search only within discovered scope; expand scope via Graph, not grep cascades.
- Consultation & Edge Case Discussion Before Planning: If the user's prompt includes an engineering inquiry, trade-off question, architectural validation, asks to study/research missing scenarios or surface edge cases before starting (e.g. "study this carefully", "find missing scenarios/edge cases before starting"), or asks for confirmation before starting (e.g. "confirm with me first", "is this logic sound or best-practice?", "should we do A or B?"), the agent MUST fully discuss, analyze, and present the findings directly in plain chat BEFORE invoking `workflow.py draft` or drafting any plan. When asked to surface edge cases or examine missing scenarios, the agent MUST present and discuss a comprehensive breakdown of all identified edge cases directly in chat first, and await developer alignment before drafting any implementation plan. Never swallow consultation questions or edge-case discovery into an immediate plan artifact. Only after the developer confirms the direction or says to proceed (e.g. "start", "write the plan"), begin the discovery and planning workflow.
- Inspection vs. Mutation Invariant: Inquiries asking to check, verify, examine, or understand existing flow/logic (e.g. "check if...", "how does X work?") are strictly read-only investigations: use read tools and report findings in chat. Never invoke `workflow.py draft`, create plans, or mutate code unless explicitly instructed to implement changes.
- Pre-Planning Clarification: Missing requirements, edge cases, or domain ambiguities MUST be clarified interactively before drafting the plan; guessing or silently assuming missing scenarios is strictly forbidden.
- Plan Approval Clarity: The approval question is the request: never add a separate sentence asking for approval (no "Review the plan above" line). If the developer replies with approval in chat, proceed immediately; never wait for a nonexistent button.
- Unified Chat & Question UI/UX (Language-Adaptive): Match the developer's active conversation language dynamically (never hardcode a fixed language) and use the same 5 canonical Markdown card layouts across every task: (1) Plan Approval Card (`[plan.md](<URI>)` + bold-labeled `APPROVAL_BRIEF` bullets), (2) Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |`), (3) Review Verdict Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Verdict | Findings |`), (4) 3-Section Mobile Walkthrough (`Navigation & Preconditions`, `| # | Action | Expected Result |` table, `Edge Cases`), and (5) Commit & Delivery Card (verified file list + fenced Conventional Commit block). In any right-to-left (RTL) language, start every line/bullet with a word in that language and wrap every code symbol, file name, command, and English term in `` `backticks` ``.
- Developer Decisions via `ask_question`: Every DEVELOPER_ACTION (plan approval, `MOBILE_VALIDATION_DECISION`, device sign-off, `DEVELOPER_GIT_COMMIT_REQUIRED`, a gate or finding that needs the developer) is asked with `ask_question`, and the question text is self-contained: the plan approval question follows the `APPROVAL_QUESTION` line that `draft`/`revise` print (with `--json`, inside `approval_material`; after a revise of an approved plan it asks only about the change) (first `PLAN_DOCUMENT_URI` as a clickable markdown link to `plan.md`; then the `APPROVAL_BRIEF` lines translated, each said once, as markdown with bold labels, never in a code block, where links cannot be clicked; no second summary, task id, hashes, modules or surface lists; when the developer asked for the change, never ask first whether to revise), never plan.json or raw command output; the sign-off question carries the numbered walkthrough steps with the expected result of each; the commit question carries the exact files (naming any the router says also hold the developer's earlier edits), a suggested Conventional Commit message and the options "Committed - verify and deliver" / "Request changes" / "Cancel task". On "Committed", run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task deliver --repo . --task-id <id>` yourself; never ask the developer to run `deliver`. Every question is markdown with bold labels and no emoji; in a right-to-left language, start each line with a word in that language and put code names, file names, values and English terms in backticks.
- Plan Content: pass `--approach`, `--risks` and `--device-strategy` (numbered phone steps, each with its expected result) to `draft`; a `PLAN_GAPS=` line means run `revise` with them before asking for approval.
- Updating the harness: when the developer asks to update it, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py update-info` and follow what it prints; never search for another way (package managers, the web, copying files).
- Cancel is the developer's: only when the developer asks in chat, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task cancel --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<their words>"`; never cancel on your own, and never run resume, revise, or edit files to undo the work (the files stay as they are). Up to 3 concurrent live tasks with disjoint `--expected-files` may coexist in the same worktree (`task draft --task-id <new-id>` and `task switch --task-id <id>`); never demand cancelling an active task to start a disjoint task.
- Developer-written reasons: when a gate asks the developer to run a command with `--proof-reference`, keep the `"<why ...>"` placeholder for the developer to fill in; never write their reason for them.
- Review Outcome Reporting: After `review finalize`, tell the developer each reviewer's verdict and finding count (and every blocking finding) before continuing.
- Gate vs Developer Instruction: When a gate refuses something the developer explicitly asked for or already decided (inline text, a rejected option, removing existing app behaviour), stop and ask with `ask_question`, quoting the gate message and the consequence of each option. Never switch to a different approach, or to an option the developer rejected, on your own.
- Deferred Translations: For text another locale will translate later, add the base string with `l10n-todo="true"`; never copy base-language text into another locale's file and never use `translatable="false"` for user-facing text.
- Durable Context: Record, update, or remove a project note or developer instruction (`context note` / `context instruct`) only when the developer asks for a durable project rule. Never paste the developer's raw conversational phrasing verbatim: clarify any ambiguity first, then organize, detail, and translate the rule into clear, self-contained English before saving so any future model can understand it easily. A decision for the current task belongs in the plan (`workflow.py revise ... --risks "<decision>"`).
- Preflight Scope: `preflight` runs inside an active task only; before a plan exists use discovery commands.
- Multi-Phase Execution: Multi-phase plans execute sequentially and autonomously. Single intake approval covers all phases; never pause or ask developer between phases.
- Strict Verification Order: The Verification Plan MUST use the 6-step headings (1. preflight -> 2. unit tests -> 3. routed reviewers -> 4. device install -> 5. mobile walkthrough -> 6. verify). The agent MUST wait for ALL routed specialist reviewers to finish, record their responses, and verify ZERO blocking findings BEFORE running `assemble` or starting device installation. Starting assemble or device deployment while any reviewer is still running is strictly forbidden.
- Reviewer Dispatch: 100% autonomous. Launch routed reviewers in parallel via subagents immediately; never pause or ask for permission. Whenever listing or reporting dispatched, running, or completed reviewers in chat, always display each reviewer alongside its active model from `reviewer_models` (e.g., `bug-reviewer-agent [gemini-3.8-flash-high]`, `security-reviewer-agent [inherit]`).
- Review Protocol V2: On reactive reviewer completion, record trusted reviewer results with `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>`. Once all routed reviewers complete, finalize aggregate review evidence with `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review finalize --task <id>`. Clean reviews with findings: [] are recognized as PASS. Intermediate scratch files are forbidden.
- Hard decisions before planning: Before `draft`, when the task carries a design, migration, backward-compatibility or security decision (Room schema, exported components, permissions, public contracts), ask the developer about it with `ask_question`; for a Room change ask about an existing destructive fallback, users on older schema versions and downgrade first. Carry resolved answers into the plan; do not repeat resolved questions or persist inferred conventions.
- Continuous execution: After approval, follow `task status --next --json` until terminal completion or a real developer/environment boundary, without stopping between steps.
- Finding Adjudication: If a reviewer reports a false positive, adjudicate via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task validate-finding --repo . --task-id <id> --finding-id <id> --status FALSE_POSITIVE --reason "<rationale>"`. The technical rationale is embedded directly into `review-package.md`, allowing re-reviewers to accept the explanation without manual bypass. A validation is an unverified note for the next review round; it never clears a finding. To keep code a HIGH/CRITICAL finding disputes, ask the developer.
- Zero-Polling Invariant: Never poll background tasks or subagents in a loop using `manage_task(Action='status')`, `manage_subagents(Action='list')`, or `schedule`. Yield execution and wait for reactive messages from the system.
- Existing File Edit Invariant: Never use `write_file(Overwrite=true)` to modify any existing file in the project; always use `edit_file` to modify only the targeted sections and preserve commented-out code and original line endings.
- Harness Immutability & Diagnostic Protocol: The harness engine under `.agents/**` is immutable developer infrastructure. If any harness command or verification gate crashes with a Python traceback or system error, the agent is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from attempting to edit or patch files in `.agents/**`. Instead, stop immediately, report the exact traceback and root cause to the developer, and await instructions. The same applies when a harness command fails with a message the router gives no next action for: report it; do not read `.agents/scripts/**` to debug the harness.
- Task Resumption: If a task becomes BLOCKED or fixes are needed during verification, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task resume --repo . --task-id <id>` to return to implementation.
- {{GIT_POLICY}}
- Independent Reviews: Reviewer roles selected by policy MUST be executed independently via subagents. The lead agent is strictly forbidden from self-certifying reviews using `record_review.py --verdict PASS` on HIGH/CRITICAL or sensitive changes; evaluations must come from actual reviewer runs.
- Antigravity Planning Lifecycle: The interactive Proceed button appears ONLY on initial task plan approval. Subsequent updates show only Review. Never tell the developer to click 'Proceed' on follow-ups or bug fixes during active tasks; execute, compile, and deploy directly. When the developer approves in chat (e.g. replies with an approval in any language), the agent MUST immediately record approval via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` (which atomically transitions directly to `IMPLEMENTING`); NEVER instruct the developer to run PowerShell commands manually.
- 6-Tier Dynamic Risk Model: Review policy (`review_policy.py`) evaluates changes into 6 risk tiers (`T0_TRIVIAL` through `T5_CRITICAL`) and is the sole runtime authority for risk tier, required gates, reviewer roster, and device requirements. Execute exactly the policy-resolved roster; when reviewers are omitted by policy, do not dispatch subagents.
- Next-Action Command Router: Follow the returned next_action or NEXT_ACTION/NEXT_REASON directly. Only when the action/payload is missing, query `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task status --task-id <id> --next --brief --json`. Never repeat status after a complete routed result. Once implementation is finished, `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py verify-steps --task-id <id> --host <actual-host>` runs consecutive deterministic steps and stops at failures, reviews or decisions; STOPPED is not task completion.
- Mobile Verification Walkthrough & Device Verification: When device verification is required, Next Action router presents the decision (`MOBILE_VALIDATION_DECISION`). Execute `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device install-start` to install and launch on target device. If the developer explicitly chooses to skip device verification, record honest skip evidence via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device skip-validation --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`. Honest skip records `status: "SKIPPED"` (never synthetic PASS). When installation succeeds, output a complete, numbered mobile verification walkthrough (Navigation path, Preconditions, User actions, Expected results, Edge cases) in chat BEFORE asking for sign-off. Once developer replies with explicit PASS, record device sign-off via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device signoff --task-id <id> --verdict PASS --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`. Never run signoff before developer replies.
- Linked Zoho Sprints Integration: When a task plan includes an approved `zoho_link`, sync task start with `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py zoho start-sync --task-id <id>` after approval, and sync delivery status/report with `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py zoho delivery-sync --task-id <id>` after developer git commit. All Zoho task descriptions and comments must strictly obey any Zoho Sprints formatting, language, HTML template, and No-Code-Leak rules defined in `.agents/project-context/project-notes.md`.
- Context Management Actions: Updating project context, recording architectural conventions, or adding/editing/removing domain notes is an administrative context action, NOT an Android code delivery task. Never paste the developer's raw conversational phrasing verbatim: clarify any ambiguity first, then structure, detail, and translate the rule into clear, self-contained English before running `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<structured-english-note>"` (`--replace "<old>"` / `--remove "<old>"`) or `context instruct` (`--supersedes <id>` / `--remove <id>`). Always adhere to `.agents/project-context/project-notes.md` across discovery, planning, implementation, review, and tracker updates.
- Review Host Binding:
  - In Antigravity, prepare verification with:
    `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity`
  - Never claim Review Protocol V2 unless `current-run.json` says `review_protocol_version = 2`.
- Reviewer Brief Inputs: Read the canonical `next_action.inputs` in JSON status output (plain output exposes the same payload once as `NEXT_ACTION_INPUTS`). Use only its dispatch reviewer roster. For each role pass `reviewer_prompts[role]` (a one-line pointer to the current brief, bound by its hash) as `Prompt` and do not open brief files; only for a role without a pointer, pass its exact `review_execution_profile.reviewers[role].brief_content`. Never a summary, a prior run's brief, or the whole execution profile. Missing or unreadable briefs block dispatch. After dispatch, follow WAIT/completion/retry actions; do not launch the roster again.
- Exact Reviewer Dispatch Procedure (Antigravity):
  1. Run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task status --task-id <id> --next --json` (or `workflow.py status`).
  2. If code == DISPATCH_REVIEWERS:
     - if `before_first_dispatch` (`SELECT_REVIEW_MODEL`) is present, ask the developer with `ask_question` using the 5 choices (`flash-dynamic-task`, `flash-dynamic-once`, `inherit-task`, `inherit-once`, `hybrid-smart-task`) and run its `command_template` before launching subagents;
     - use exactly the returned reviewer set;
     - one invoke_subagent call;
     - for each reviewer:
         TypeName = exact reviewer role
         Role = exact reviewer role
         Prompt = reviewer_prompts[role] (one line; do not open the brief)
         Workspace = inherit (or omit if host default is used consistently)
         Model = "flash" if `reviewer_models[role]` starts with `gemini-3.8-flash-`; otherwise omit `model`/`Model` (INHERIT_PARENT_BY_OMISSION)
     - do not invent reasoning fields;
     - in chat, list each dispatched/completed reviewer with its active model from `reviewer_models` (`<role> [<model>]`).
  3. Yield; do not poll.
  4. On reactive completion, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` (repeat `--reviewer` and `--execution-id` in one call to complete all ready reviewers together).
  5. On RETRY_REVIEW_PROTOCOL, execute the exact router-provided send_message.
  6. On REVIEW_ENV_BLOCKED / REVIEW_PROFILE_BLOCKED / REVIEW_PROTOCOL_BLOCKED, stop reviewer flow and report blocker.
  7. After all completed, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review finalize --task <id>` (if not already auto-finalized).
  No legacy PASS token. No EVIDENCE footer. No self-certification.
- Exact Scoped Phase Review V2 Procedure (Antigravity):
  1. On `BUILD_PHASE_REVIEW_PACKAGE`: run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py phase-review package --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>`.
  2. On `DISPATCH_PHASE_REVIEWERS`:
     - use exactly the returned reviewer set;
     - one `invoke_subagent` call;
     - for each reviewer:
         TypeName = exact reviewer role
         Role = exact reviewer role
         Prompt = exact current phase brief
         Workspace = inherit (or omit if host default is used consistently)
         Model = "flash" if `reviewer_models[role]` starts with `gemini-3.8-flash-`; otherwise omit `model`/`Model` (INHERIT_PARENT_BY_OMISSION)
     - do not invent reasoning fields;
     - in chat, list each dispatched/completed phase reviewer with its active model from `reviewer_models` (`<role> [<model>]`).
  3. Yield; do not poll.
  4. On reactive reviewer completion, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py phase-review complete --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` (repeat `--reviewer` and `--execution-id` in one call when multiple phase reviewers finish together).
  5. On `RETRY_PHASE_REVIEW_PROTOCOL`, execute the exact router-provided `send_message`.
  6. On `PHASE_REVIEW_ENV_BLOCKED` / `PHASE_REVIEW_PROTOCOL_BLOCKED` / `PHASE_REVIEW_LEDGER_BLOCKED`, stop reviewer flow and report blocker.
  7. After all phase reviewers completed, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py phase-review finalize --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>`.
  8. Advance to next phase via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task begin-next-phase --task-id <id>` (no second approval needed).

Antigravity may load `.agents/hooks.json`; Gemini CLI may be rule-enforced only. Report the detected enforcement tier honestly.

## Canonical Command Catalog & Sequential Lifecycle

Execute commands in this strict sequential order. Every command is fully specified with all required arguments:

| Step | Lifecycle Stage | Canonical Command | Description & Parameter Rules |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | **Discovery** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` (or `--symbol <name>`) | Bounded AST slice for target file/symbol |
| 1b | **Feature / Find Graph** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py graph --feature <name> --json` (or `--find <Symbol>`) | Fast AST/symbol feature graph analysis |
| 2 | **Draft Plan** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task draft --repo . --task-id <id> --outcome "<outcome>" --kind <AUTO\|BUG\|FEATURE\|REFACTOR> --expected-files <paths>` | Create task plan. Required: `--task-id`, `--outcome`, `--expected-files <comma-separated paths from discovery>` (T0 resource/string/doc-only plans may omit it). Optional: `--kind`, `--expected-modules`, `--expected-surfaces`, `--architecture-target-scope <file>` (in hybrid codebases to target/preserve specific screen), `--architecture-intent <NEW_FEATURE\|NEW_SCREEN\|EXISTING_CHANGE>` |
| 3 | **Approve Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` | Record chat approval & atomically transition to IMPLEMENTING |
| 4 | **(Compat) Begin Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task begin --repo . --task-id <id>` | Idempotent begin compatibility command |
| 4b | **Zoho Start Sync** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py zoho start-sync --task-id <id>` | Sync In progress status to linked Zoho item (when plan has approved zoho_link) |
| 4c | **Task Handoff** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task handoff --task-id <id>` | Freeze WIP checkpoint for safe worktree switch |
| 4d | **Reconcile Handoff** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task reconcile-handoff --task-id <id>` | Validate developer WIP commit and update lineage |
| 4e | **Phase Package** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py phase-review package --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>` | Build immutable phase review package markdown and lean briefs |
| 4f | **Phase Review Complete** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py phase-review complete --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` | Record trusted specialist phase review completion |
| 4g | **Phase Review Finalize** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py phase-review finalize --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>` | Finalize phase review evidence and substate |
| 5 | **Compile Check** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py compile` | Compile without tests before prepare-verification |
| 6 | **Prepare Verification** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity` | Freeze review package & transition to VERIFYING. Required: `--task-id` |
| 7 | **Preflight Gate** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py preflight` | Deterministic check: room, fast ktlint, string parity. Zero flags required |
| 8 | **Unit Tests Gate** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/run_tests_gate.py` | Run unit tests gate (when required by policy). Zero flags required |
| 9 | **Review Package** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/review_package.py --task-id <id>` (or auto-detects active task) | Generate immutable review package markdown. `--task-id` is optional |
| 10 | **Record Review** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` | Record trusted specialist reviewer completion |
| 10b | **Validate Finding** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task validate-finding --repo . --task-id <id> --finding-id <id> --status <FALSE_POSITIVE\|CONFIRMED> --reason "<text>"` | Validate reviewer finding. `--reason` mandatory for FALSE_POSITIVE |
| 10c | **Resume Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task resume --repo . --task-id <id>` | Resume to IMPLEMENTING if fixes needed. Required: `--task-id` |
| 10d | **Finalize Reviews** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review finalize --task <id>` | Finalize aggregate review evidence once all routed reviewers complete |
| 11 | **Assemble** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` | Build debug APK (ONLY after all reviewers pass or REVIEWERS=NONE; derived assemble task) |
| 12 | **Device Deploy / Skip** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device install-start` (or `device skip-validation --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`) | Install & launch on device (when required), or record explicit developer skip |
| 12b | **Screen Capture** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/capture_screen.py --name <prefix>` | Optional screenshot verification proof |
| 12c | **Device Signoff** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device signoff --task-id <id> --verdict PASS --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` | Record explicit developer device verification sign-off |
| 13 | **Final Verify** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task verify --repo . --task-id <id>` | Read-only delivery verification check. Required: `--task-id` |
| 14 | **Complete Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task complete --repo . --task-id <id>` | Transition task to READY_FOR_DELIVERY. Required: `--task-id` |
| 15 | **Deliver Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task deliver --repo . --task-id <id>` | Finalize delivery state after git commit. Required: `--task-id` |
| 15b | **Zoho Delivery Sync** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py zoho delivery-sync --task-id <id>` | Sync delivery report & resolution to linked Zoho item (when plan has zoho_link) |
| - | **Context Note** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<structured-english-note>"` (`--replace "<old>"` / `--remove "<old>"`) | Add, replace, or remove a structured English architectural convention/note |
| - | **Context Instruct** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context instruct "<structured-english-instruction>" --scope "<scope>" --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --strength REQUIREMENT` (`--supersedes <id>` / `--remove <id>`) | Add, supersede, or remove a scoped developer instruction in developer-instructions.json |

For optional criteria, journeys, and metrics, follow the kernel and canonical router.
